# LAN upload

An unknown phone is rejected. A QR payload expires and is not reused after the device is forgotten.

Uploaded bytes become a domain image only after a size check and a successful decode. The computer assigns the stored file name. The client filename is never a path.

Images stay on the LAN. There is no account and no internet relay.

Settings updates are partial patches. Unknown keys are rejected. `history_retention_days` accepts only 1 through 90. Lowering it purges images older than the new limit immediately.
